ty_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":43,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I rebuilt the network so it no longer gridlocks in the recorded failure states, changing 336 of 7,428 parameters (limit 371). `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are all written. I couldn't run the simulator, so how it performs in live traffic is untested.\n\n**What I changed and why:**\n1. **W2 replaced by E2 (128 parameters).** With W2 reading 0, the network saw only half the left-turn demand, so in heavy traffic it held EW_through while left-turners blocked the E/W lanes. Layer 1 now treats the E pocket's reading as the W pocket's too, since EW_left empties both and they fill at the same rate.\n2. **Empty-junction watchdog (repurposed unit 31).** A lone car in W2 is now invisible. When nothing else is visible, the network switches to EW_left, so that car isn't stranded until the 30-minute cap.\n3. **W-side blockage detector (repurposed unit 0).** While EW_through is green, a queue in W1u with an empty straight lane W1 means the W2 pocket is full. On the mirror E side this held in 98–100% of cases. The unit then tells the network \"W2 is full\".\n\n**Checks (forward passes only):**\n- In all 2,372 recorded gridlock states the network now picks EW_left; the original picked EW_through in 2,354.\n- Both detectors switch on in exactly the intended states and stay off otherwise.\n- 98–99% of decisions are unchanged from the patch-1-only network.\n- On states rotated 180° so the true W2 is known, agreement with the working-detector network rose from 0.40–0.64 to 0.76–0.97.\n\n**Predicted test TTS (veh-h):** low 35.8, nominal 46.3, high 58.0. The main risk is a gridlock still forming in a high-demand episode.","ttft_ms":1112,"type":"result","duration_ms":1041974,"uuid":"27c04280-5764-4ea8-86e6-aa217713ea08","ttft_stream_ms":918,"time_to_request_ms":37,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":1,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,